novelty_contribution:
{
  "theoretical_contribution": "This study introduces a systematic framework for analyzing communication strategies within Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning (MARL) for dynamic resource allocation, establishing a causal relationship between communication efficiency and coordination among agents. It posits that enhanced communication mechanisms directly improve resource allocation outcomes in mobile-edge cloud environments.",
  "technical_contribution": "The research develops and implements specific communication protocols tailored for MARL agents, which are designed to optimize coordination and resource allocation efficiency. These protocols are integrated into existing open-source MARL frameworks, providing a new method for training agents in dynamic environments.",
  "empirical_contribution": "Through a six-month evaluation period, the study generates empirical findings that quantify the impact of various communication strategies on user throughput and Quality of Service (QoS) metrics, offering new insights into the adaptability of MARL algorithms under changing user demands and network conditions.",
  "practical_deployment_contribution": "The research provides deployment guidelines for implementing the proposed MARL framework in real-world mobile-edge cloud systems, including recommendations for configuring communication strategies to enhance resource allocation performance, thereby addressing practical challenges faced by cloud service providers."
}

